# Issue Tracking Process (Freshworks)

This project uses Freshworks for tracking bugs, enhancements, and feature requests.

---

## Creating an Issue

1. Log into Freshworks.
2. Select the Cybersecurity Analysis Tool project.
3. Click "New Tickdet".
4. Provide:
   - Clear title
   - Detailed description
   - Steps to reproduce (if bug)
   - Acceptance criteria (if feature)

---

## Issue Workflow

Issues move through the following stages:

Open → In Progress → Resolved → Closed

---

## Assigning Issues

- Each issue is assigned to a responsible developer.
- Priority levels are set based on severity.

---

## Linking GitHub Commits to Issues

When committing changes related to an issue, reference the issue number:

Example:

git commit -m "Add error handling to log analysis script. Fixes #12"

This ensures traceability between development and issue tracking.

---

## Benefits of Issue Tracking

- Maintains accountability
- Provides audit trail
- Improves project organization
- Supports structured security management
